From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: expose the fixed O82 10-bpc link to userspace

The O82 panel reports display_info.bpc=10, but KWin obtains its color
resolution capability from the max bpc connector property. Advertise only
the existing OEM RGB101010/DSC 10-bpc contract. No receiver mode or optical
12-bit/FRC support is established by this property.

Initialize atomic state before the property helper writes it, as required
by this kernel's bridge connector implementation, and propagate failures.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_manager.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_manager.c
@@ -827,6 +827,16 @@ int msm_dsi_manager_connector_init(struct msm_dsi *msm_dsi,
 		return PTR_ERR(connector);
 	}
 	if (dsi_bridge->o82_panel) {
+		if (!connector->state) {
+			connector->funcs->reset(connector);
+			if (!connector->state)
+				return -ENOMEM;
+		}
+		/* O82 has one qualified transport depth, including DSC input. */
+		ret = drm_connector_attach_max_bpc_property(connector, 10, 10);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+
 		ret = drm_connector_attach_vrr_capable_property(connector);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
